# Fast local stack

When the user asks to start / bring up / make running the app, services, or local stack:

1. Run this immediately from `LocalHyperMart` (do not rediscover how to start):

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\start-dev.ps1
```

2. If they changed Java code since the last JAR build, add `-Rebuild`.
3. If they only want backend: `-SkipWeb`. To free RAM later: `.\scripts\stop-dev.ps1` (Docker stays up unless `-Down`).
4. Do not use `mvn spring-boot:run` or `mvn clean install` for everyday start — the script uses existing fat JARs and `java -jar`.
5. After start, run `.\scripts\health-check.ps1` only if the start script still reported DOWN services.

Repeat asks should take seconds (Docker + JARs already present), not a Maven rebuild.
